Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:37:03 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - fail the stop when AWF cannot confirm a storage

AwfEngine.closeAll() now returns how many Aurora World Fabric storages
could not be confirmed at shutdown (failed, refused by the shutdown
deadline, or sent but unanswered), counting those closed earlier by
their world's region save. A non-zero count sets abnormalExit, so the
process exits with status 70 instead of 0 after logging the
AWF-SHUTDOWN-INCOMPLETE alert; an operator's restart script or panel
sees the stop did not save everything. With no AWF storage open it
returns 0 and nothing changes.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java b/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
index f6332288d3aa311e2ed911324850f606f443b237..a32d4c59630f8c0b22201c6d9d831249a1ce82ba 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
@@ -1173,7 +1173,7 @@ public abstract class MinecraftServer extends ReentrantBlockableEventLoop<TickTa
         LOGGER.info("Waiting for all RegionFile I/O tasks to complete...");
         ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.patches.chunk_system.io.MoonriseRegionFileIO.flush((MinecraftServer)(Object)this);
         LOGGER.info("All RegionFile I/O tasks to complete");
-        dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.awf.AwfEngine.closeAll(); // SourbyCraft - Aurora World Fabric: every save has reached its storage
+        if (dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.awf.AwfEngine.closeAll() > 0) this.abnormalExit = true; // SourbyCraft - Aurora World Fabric: every save has reached its storage; an unconfirmed storage fails the stop (exit 70)
         if ((Object)this instanceof net.minecraft.server.dedicated.DedicatedServer) {
             ca.spottedleaf.moonrise.common.util.MoonriseCommon.haltExecutors();
         }
